{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Noel felt like the strongest next choice because its Christmas repertoire connects directly to my repeated holiday listening.",
    "Cheek to Cheek, Josh Groban, I Dreamed A Dream, and Michael Bublé appealed to my interest in melodic singing and classic vocal performances, even though I would only choose Noel today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Adele albums and In The Lonely Hour did not give me the holiday or vocal-harmony connection I wanted on this visit.",
    "Duets did not give me enough information about the performers or songs to judge whether it matched my interests, and How Can It Be offered no clear connection to what I wanted."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seemed to treat an interest in strong singers as enough reason to recommend a broad range of vocal albums.",
    "An appealing solo voice or a duet format alone does not make an album as relevant to me as familiar holiday repertoire."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated Christmas-album listening deserved more weight in understanding why Noel stood out from the other vocal albums.",
    "My latest interaction with The New Old Fashioned also matters: vocal-group harmonies can interest me beyond Christmas music, but that does not mean any solo pop album will appeal."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in vocal music but stretched it too broadly beyond the holiday repertoire and harmonies that made one choice compelling today."
}"}
